  "pillars": {
    "title": "Pillars",
    "images": {
      "big": "/assets/images/biglittle.jpg",
      "atlanta": "/assets/images/atlantatrip.jpg",
      "socialevent": "/assets/images/socials.jpg"
    },
    "items": [
      {
        "title": "Community",
        "subtitle": "KUSA Big/Little, Atlanta Trip, Social Events",
        "description": "Through various events and programs, KUSA aims to connect with the community, both internally within our own organization and externally with broader Gainesville and beyond!",
        "image": "/assets/images/happyTeam.jpeg",
        "key": "community"
      },
      {
        "title": "Culture",
        "subtitle": "Through GBMs, as well as Chuseok and Seollal Shows, we share Korea's culture",
        "description": "KUSA GBMs focus on teaching Korean culture and serve as a welcoming and interactive session for members to learn and celebrate various aspects of Korean traditions, language, cuisine, music, and contemporary culture. These meetings often include cultural presentations, fun games, and opportunities to try Korean food. Check out some of our previous GBMs below!",
        "description2":  "We also have a cultural show each Fall and Spring semester, for Chuseok and Seollal. Chuseok is Korean Thanksgiving and it is the time to celebrate the harvest, family, and ancestors. Seollal is Korean Lunar New Year and is celebrated by honoring ancestors and playing traditional games. In our shows, we incorporate dancing, skits, and games to share our traditions and stories.",
        "image": "/assets/images/culture.jpg",
        "key": "culture"
      },
      {
        "title": "Education",
        "subtitle": "Korean Language Program (KLP) and other workshops",
        "description": "Each semester our KLP chairs host 1-2 language workshops where anyone can come to learn various Korean words, phrases, and basic grammer. Since Korean culture is rapidly spreading globally, the Korean language of Hangul is more relevant and useful than ever before. We also host other workshops for learning dance and volleyball! Come learn a new skill with KUSA!",
        "image": "/assets/images/klp.jpg",
        "key": "education"
      },
      {
        "title": "Philanthrophy",
        "subtitle": "Through Korean Kids and Orphanage Outreach Mission (KKOOM) we help provide access to education for Korean youth",
        "description": "Korean Kids and Orphanage Outreach Mission (KKOOM) provides access to education for Korean youth, such as funding for preschool and college scholarships. KKOOM also sponsors and hosts holiday celebrations, summer activities, and other events throughout the year which help the children and young adults have fun and learn life skills. Additionally, KKOOM gives gifts of clothing, household items, and other tangible support to meet the basic needs at Korean children's homes. To learn more about KKOOM and help their mission, please visit their website!",
        "image": "/assets/images/kkoom.png",
        "key": "philanthrophy"
      }
    ]
  },
